<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2638" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰπύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εῖα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ύ</span>, 
			Ep.
		 and Lyr. Adj., rare in Trag., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>high and steep</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> mostly of cities on rocky heights, esp. of Troy, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.485
			</span></i>, al.; of hills, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.603
			</span></i>; later of the sky, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					3.36
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρανός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					845
				</span></i>
			; <i>on high</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδῶν αἰ. ἰωή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					682
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁψαμένη βρόχον αἰπύν</span>
			<i>hanging high</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.278
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>sheer, utter</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ.
			ὄλεθρος</span> freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, death being regarded as <i>the plunge from a high
				precipice</i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόνος αἰ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.843
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).42
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκότος</span>
			<i>utter</i> darkness, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				228
			</span></i>; of passions, etc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. χόλος</span>
			<i>towering</i> wrath, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.223
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλος αἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				66
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				589
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰπυτάτη σοφίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.354
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); <i>arduous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.601
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				16.651
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰπύ οἱ ἐσσεῖται</span>
			'twill be <i>hard work</i> for him, <i><span class="en">
				13.317
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
